# Source-archive SHA256 checksums for this repository's own release tags.
#
# Format: HASH  IDENTIFIER
# (two spaces between hash and identifier, like sha256sum output)
#
# Source provenance must come from this recorded metadata, not from a digest
# computed during the release run: a digest that a release job derives from a
# live download anchors nothing, and GitHub's generated tag archives are not
# guaranteed to stay byte-identical, so the same tag can yield a different
# digest later.
#
# Record an entry after the tag is published, with the maintainer script (the
# entry lands in a later commit, so the tag's own tree is unaffected):
#   bash packaging/scripts/record-source-archive-digest.sh v0.9.2
# The script downloads the tag archive, requires it to match any existing
# entry, and writes the reviewed line into this file. Commit the result.
#
# The release workflow looks the tag up here and records the digest it finds in
# the release manifest. It warns, without failing, when the tag has no entry yet,
# because an entry can only be created after the run publishes the archive.
#
# Identifier convention: source-<tag>          (e.g. source-v0.9.2)
